			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2252316">
									

<p>I'm close to liking this one, but I'm a no-vote for now. There are some tone issues that I will let others with more time analyze, but for me the real hurdle is its missing that ever-elusive hook that takes something from good to great. Find something that makes these things more than just lava monsters. I will say that you're on the right track with the Euclid thing- more dangerous is not necessarily more interesting. I'd suggest that you might expand a little on the documentary side of things: what do we know about their life cycles, do they nest anywhere, are they important to plate tectonics or the health of the earth's mantle and core (and thus the magnetosphere)? There's a lot you can play with here.</p>

