			<div class="content" id="post-content-2556143">
									

<p>Personally, I enjoy this piece, but I don't actually see why these creatures would be hidden by the Foundation.</p>
<p>Unless they aren't naturally occuring on Earth, they're really just mundane, if highly unusual, animals, and probably don't warrant attempted containment or occlusion.</p>
<p>Also, the presence of defence mechanisms suggest that there are predatory lifeforms, or unique hazards, in the Earth's mantel. Magma expulsion implies retreat, and crying implies parental care after birth. Is that your intention?</p>

